  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member whose stored password no longer matches (a password changed elsewhere), I want the app to tell me my session expired instead of showing \"no information\", so that I log in again. The captures of #168, #173 and #281 now show what HFR answers to such a session.\n\n### Facts (captures, docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md §6c LOT-044, LOT-047, LOT-024)\n\n- A jar with the account's `md_user`/`md_id` and a `md_passs` HFR refuses gets the **same bytes** on the home page, `forum1f.php?owntopic=1` and profile pages 1 and 5 (`R70a`–`R70d`): 200, no redirect, no `Set-Cookie`, `.hop` \"Identifiants invalides !\", `Refresh: 1; url=/unlog.php?config=hfr.inc`.\n- Without cookies, profile pages 1 and 5 answer `.hop` \"Mot de passe incorrect !\" with `Refresh: 1; url=../login.php?config=hfr.inc` (`R71a`, `R71b`).\n- `GET /unlog.php?config=hfr.inc` without `codehex` does nothing (`R72a`, `R72b`): following the stale page's refresh with the account jar must not be read as a logout, and is not needed.\n- Every logged-in answer sets `md_user` and `md_passs` twice: the value for `.hardware.fr`, then `deleted` for `.forum.hardware.fr`, expired in 1970 (`R74` note). That `deleted` is not a logout.\n\n### Scope\n\n1. `SessionRefreshFlow` (LOT-044): the `R70c` page (profile page 1, stale) becomes a `SessionExpiry` case (today `unconfirmed`); `R71b` stays \"no session\". Match the `.hop` sentence and the refresh target, not the size.\n2. A test that a refresh whose answer carries the doubled pair of `R74` (value for `.hardware.fr`, expired `deleted` for `.forum.hardware.fr`) keeps the account logged in (`userKey` still the pseudo): the LOT-044 spec fears `identityNotConfirmed` there.\n3. `MPUnreadPoll` (LOT-047): decide whether `R70a` stays `nil` (no information) or reports the expiry through the same classifier; the LOT-092 check-updates flow (#184) consumes both answers (`R70a` home, `R70b` flags page).\n4. Update the \"Pending capture\" sections of `docs/lots/LOT-044-session-health.md` and `docs/lots/LOT-047-mp-unread-poll.md`.\n\nFiles: `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRClient/` (session refresh, MP poll), their tests, the two specs. No HFR request needed: the captures are in the corpus.\n\nRefs #168, #173, #281, #282, #283\n",
